    "notes": "Two sessions: February 7-9, 1956 and March 27, 1956, both in Hollywood. Sources consulted (Wikipedia, AllMusic, Discogs, Bregman's own site) give the city but never the studio, so the site record is city-level with epistemic inf and no slug invented for a named room. Engineer is not credited in any source consulted (explicit null). Personnel comes from the CD-reissue liner notes as transcribed in the Wikipedia personnel table; the string section list there is explicitly marked incomplete, and the source states which tracks each wind/brass/rhythm section plays, which is what the per-track assignments here reproduce — no track assignment was inferred beyond those stated sections. Paul Smith is credited on piano/celeste on all tracks except 2.11. Track 27 (Night and Day) therefore has no piano. Three 1997-reissue alternate takes are listed with no session date and epistemic unk. Rating claims (Grammy Hall of Fame, National Recording Registry, Penguin, EPM, AllMusic, Rolling Stone) are all carried by source S1."
